Majestrious foe, thy lament's deep as winter's frost,
Upon this field I'll stand where hope and iron rest;
Hail thine, O adversary, and bear this challenge cast.

I stand upon this verdant earth with my own eyes,
And watch the trees as they shed gold in autumn's breath,
Their silence stark against the coming cold air;

